onse across 67.25 to 201.75 mg.","status":"proposed","supporting_observed_ids":[],"why_it_matters_for_model_learning":"A measured departure would identify a condition-response failure relevant beyond this molecule; agreement would discourage spending later batches on similar loading contrasts."},{"basis":"chemical_prior","confidence":"low","contradicting_observed_ids":[],"created_round":0,"id":"H0002","last_updated_round":0,"next_discriminating_question":"At fixed 134.5 mg loading and identical carrier conditions, how do nitroacetophenone V1 and V2 change from pure EA to 1/1 and 2/1?","statement":"Increasing the PE fraction often increases retention on normal-phase silica, but the magnitude and even the observed trend can depend on structure and conditions.","status":"proposed","supporting_observed_ids":[],"why_it_matters_for_model_learning":"A controlled solvent-ratio curve can reveal where the predictor transfers solvent effects poorly without imposing a universal monotonic rule."},{"basis":"observed_data","confidence":"medium","contradicting_observed_ids":[],"created_round":2,"id":"H0003","last_updated_round":2,"next_discriminating_question":"At fixed diester loading, does the error change substantially from 10/1 through 20/1 and weaker eluents, and at fixed solvent does it recur as loading increases?","statement":"The extreme diester prediction failure is localized to a specific combination of weak eluent and high loading, rather than representing a general molecular bias for this diester.","status":"supported","supporting_observed_ids":["f7d57d8bb988f7016502","08155ffdcb0d27576050","08ae0e5f727afabf1e71"],"why_it_matters_for_model_learning":"Matched loading and solvent contrasts can teach the predictor whether the failure is driven by loading, eluent strength, or their interaction and can improve local row-distribution coverage."},{"basis":"observed_data","confidence":"medium","contradicting_observed_ids":[],"created_round":2,"id":"H0004","last_updated_round":2